From 0aa73e3d7d3d88ad7ccfa4e4928afc45d9263790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:48:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-100: the property grid laid out like WPF's -- name
 | value | marker (0.100.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "屬性表格 ... 像 wpf 讓使用者看起來條理分明". WPF's grid is two
columns and the property marker, nothing under a value. Here a value cell held
the editor, a hint, "DFM 54" and the marker, and the colour rows the 16 swatches
and the typed value: in a narrow side bar it wrapped and was cut. Now:
- three fixed columns (a colgroup: 38 % | the rest | 20 px -- with table-layout
  fixed the first row, a category band, would otherwise decide), the name on one
  line with an ellipsis, the marker in its own cell at the right edge;
- "DFM ..." shown only on a row that differs (the marker's tooltip / menu always
  has it); a note longer than a unit (px) is the ⓘ's tooltip;
- a colour row = the well + its value (typed in); BCB6's 16 colours and the
  eyedropper behind ▾;
- category headings as bands; the difference note and the note under the grid
  one line each (the rest in their tooltips).
README (the grid, the marker, the colours) and WPF_DIFF_LOG.md (0.99 commit).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 160, smoke 186, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (every row three cells with the markers in the third; the DFM value
visible only on the rows that differ; the 16 colours closed, ▾ opens them; the
system colour note in ⓘ).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
